{
 "title": "MONTAGE M FM-X Algorithm Chart (88 algorithms, 8 operators)",
 "source": "MONTAGE M Data List (montage_m_dl_H0.pdf, Yamaha), PDF page index == printed page number for these sections",
 "source_pages": [
  208,
  209,
  210,
  211
 ],
 "method": "The chart is purely graphical (pdftotext yields only the numbers). Pages were rendered with pdftoppm at 400 dpi (800 dpi for alg 65) and every cell transcribed by eye. Drawing conventions used: boxes joined by the bottom horizontal output bus are carriers; a line leaving the bottom of a box and entering the top of another (directly or via a horizontal bus) means the upper operator modulates the lower one; the thin rectangular loop beside a box is the feedback path, running from the output of the operator at its lower end back into the input of the operator at its upper end (self-feedback when both are the same box, e.g. alg 13 = 3->3; multi-operator feedback e.g. alg 12 = 5->3, alg 14 = 4->3).",
 "encoding": {
  "carriers": "operators whose output goes to the audio bus",
  "modulators": "map modulator -> list of operators it modulates",
  "feedback": "from = operator whose output is fed back, to = operator receiving it; self=true when from==to",
  "ascii": "compact text form: 'mod: a>b,c' lists targets per modulator; 'out' = carriers; 'fb' = feedback path"
 },
 "caveats": [
  "Transcribed visually; every algorithm passed a structural check (each operator is a carrier or a modulator) but individual edges have not been verified against hardware.",
  "Algorithm 65 has an ambiguous junction (see its 'uncertain' field)."
 ],
